# A bad body in a brace block inside a `for`: recovery skips to the
# block's `}`, so the `for` body goes on and the `break` below is still
# inside the loop. Two errors, both on line 7 (`while` is not an expression,
# then the missing `}` where the expression ended).
fn times(n, f) f(1) end
for x in [1, 2]
  times(1) { |i| while i end }
  break
end
